<title>UK: UK growth steady, responsible -Treasury.</title>
<headline>UK growth steady, responsible -Treasury.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>The UK is enjoying steady, responsible economic growth, the UK Treasury said after the release of average earnings and unemployment data. </p>
<p>&quot;We are creating jobs and average earnings growth is low,&quot; a Treasury spokesman said. </p>
<p>DATA RELEASED SHOWED</p>
<p>====================</p>
<p>UK OCT UNEMPLOYMENT FALLS 40,800,RATE 7.2%, SEPT UNDERLYING</p>
<p>AVG EARNINGS 4.0%</p>
<p>UK UNIT WAGE COSTS UP 5.2% IN 3 MTHS TO SEPT VS YR EARLIER</p>
<p>(AUG RVSD TO 5.1)</p>
<p>UK SEPTEMBER MANUFACTURING OVERTIME HOURS 8.67 MLN PER WEEK</p>
<p>VS 8.48 IN AUGUST</p>
<p>-- John Speck, London Newsroom +44 171 542-8663</p>
</text>
